{
  "about": "The shape of a grant name (ADR 0020, \"Grant names and the vocabulary\"; ADR 0055): three segments, <scope>:<thing>:<role>, or five, <scope>:<vendor>:<project>:<customer>:<role>. Each segment is 1 to 64 ASCII letters, digits, '-' and '_'. The scope is the first segment, the role the last, and the thing is everything between them, joined by ':', so a thing is one word or exactly three. Two segments, four, six or more, an empty segment, a wildcard and any other character are not a grant name, and a thing of two words or of four is not a thing. This is the shape only: whether a name is declared is the vocabulary's question. kits/rust/sluis-vocab (GrantName::split, valid_thing), actors/store (requires, groups), actors/signer (groups) and kits/go/groupsclaim are held to it.",
